1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
A shopper cancels after paying. Why did the warehouse still ship the order?

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:24,000
The old consumer reads loosely typed status strings. A new event slips through a permissive default.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Java twenty-one records validate event data. Sealed interfaces define exactly which event types exist.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:48,000
An exhaustive switch forces each event variant to be handled when the application is rebuilt.

5
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:60,000
But compile-time safety is not distributed safety. Guard state changes with PostgreSQL versions and a transactional outbox.

6
00:00:60,000 --> 00:00:72,000
Kafka consumers deduplicate and reject stale transitions. The customer sees cancellation pending until refund and fulfillment are resolved.
